<title>USA: First Federal Financial Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>First Federal Financial Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>IRONTON, Ohio</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.14			N/A</p>
<p> Net			     90			$79</p>
<p>Provision for</p>
<p>  loan losses		 nil			  6</p>
<p>	  SIX MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.26			N/A</p>
<p> Net			    162		     $146</p>
<p>Provision for</p>
<p>  loan losses		 nil			 12</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said no provision for loan losses was necessary in the 1997 periods as it determined that allowance for loan losses was adequate throughout the year.</p>
<p>The company said there were no shares outstanding for the second quarter and six-month 1996 periods.  On June 3, 1996 it converted from a mutual savings and loan association to a stock savings bank, known as First Federal Savings Bank of Ironton, and acquired all common stock of the bank; accordingly, 1996 results are for the association only.</p>
